# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Isolated Supabase project for the Playwright E2E suite.
#
# The end-to-end tests create and delete real rows, so they must run against a
# SEPARATE (throwaway) Supabase project — never the live demo. Copy this file
# to `.env.test.local` and fill in the values from your test project. The suite
# refuses to run unless these point at a DIFFERENT project than `.env.local`.
#
#   1. Create a second free Supabase project.
#   2. Run supabase/*.sql in its SQL editor (same order as the demo).
#   3. cp .env.test.local.example .env.test.local  (and fill in below)
#   4. npm run setup:e2e   (seeds the demo users into the test project)
#   5. npm test
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-TEST-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-test-anon-or-publishable-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-test-service-role-key
